### Template::undeclared_variables — public API with docstring example

Source: https://github.com/mitsuhiko/minijinja/blob/main/src/template.rs

The top-level method on `Template`. When `nested` is `false`, dotted accesses like `bar.baz` are collapsed to their root variable `bar`. When `nested` is `true`, the full dotted path `bar.baz` is returned.

```rust
    /// let undeclared = tmpl.undeclared_variables(false);
    /// // returns ["foo", "bar"]
    /// let undeclared = tmpl.undeclared_variables(true);
    /// // returns ["foo", "bar.baz"]
    pub fn undeclared_variables(&self, nested: bool) -> HashSet<String> {
        match parse(
            self.compiled.instructions.source(),
            self.name(),
            self.compiled.syntax_config.clone(),
            Default::default(),
        ) {
            Ok(ast) => find_undeclared(&ast, nested),
            Err(_) => HashSet::new(),
        }
    }
```

