### Run Example with Compile-Time Bundled Templates

Source: https://github.com/mitsuhiko/minijinja/blob/main/examples/embedding/README.md

Execute the example with the 'bundled' feature flag enabled to use compile-time bundled templates. This integrates templates directly into the binary.

```console
$ cargo run --features=bundled
```

### Updating to MiniJinja 3 > Mutable Execution State

Source: https://github.com/mitsuhiko/minijinja/blob/main/UPDATING.md

State mutation now relies on extensions for render-local typed Rust storage, replacing previous temporary object methods. Extensions allow data to persist through includes, blocks, and macro calls without requiring Value wrapping or mutexes. Named temporary data remains available for values that must be represented as a Value.
